# Word of Command (CR 723.2, 723.7): "the player plays that card if able". Bot2's only mana is Mox Ruby, and while Bot2
# plays the chosen card it can activate mana abilities only of lands it controls: the first Word of Command chooses
# Lightning Bolt, which Bot2 is then not able to cast, and it stays in Bot2's hand. The second chooses Bot2's Mountain on
# Bot1's turn, which no one can play (CR 305.3): it stays too. On its own turn Bot2 casts the Bolt with the Mox - the Mox
# is a mana source like any other once Word of Command is gone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Word of Command
Word of Command
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Mountain
Island x17

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Word of Command.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
? Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Colors = Red
? Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Word of Command.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Mountain)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Word of Command; Word of Command; Black Lotus
